nd it digests easily the next  snack is Greek yogurt with fruits what I  have here are frozen berries yogurt  provides you with cups and protein to  keep you energized and the added fruits  contain natural sugar for the extra  energy boost and feel free to change it  for another fruits of your choice do you  want something refreshing and life event  try this high-protein fruit smoothie  blend 1 cup of frozen berries or your  favorite fruit with one cup of water and  one scoop of your favorite protein  powder having a liquid base snack prior  to your workout will make it easy for  your body to digest and the water  content will keep your body hydrated for  a better workout performance and adding  a little bit of protein prior to your  workout will help to reduce muscle  soreness so try this presentation shake  and the next snack is dressed up oatmeal  oat milk is a popular choice for long  runs or long cardio as it provides  energy throughout your workout by  gradually releasing sugar into your  blood stream  you can choose to top your oatmeal with  fresh fruits peanut butter whole nuts  egg or cocoa powder just like what I  have here if you like something more  substantial like me why not try egg on  toast this is my regular breakfast and  also mainly my pre-workout snack 1 or 2  whole wheat toast with one hunt a slice  egg is an excellent source of protein it  keeps you satisfied and it is much  easier to digest in comparison to meat  meat is something you should try to  avoid as your pre-workout snacks as it  takes much longer to digest and it will  weigh you down during your workout  session so try a on toast  instead now if you don't have the time  and you want a quick  which you can eat on the move try dried  fruits and nuts  you can pack it in a container and bring  it out with you the healthy sugar from  dried fruits will provide you with a  quick energy boost while nuts will keep  your insulin level from dropping during  your workout session nuts are high in  healthy fat which means they take longer  to digest so if you consume a little too  many you can start to feel sluggish so  remember to have it in moderation and a  small handful is more than enough  as your pre-workout snack another quick  pre-workout snack which I often make its  my peanut butter oatmeal energy bar you  can get the full recipe from my full  vegan meal plan video this energy bar  contains all natural ingredients needed  for an excellent workouts oatmeal peanut  butter and honey for workout endurance  and for a quick energy boost so you can  make this beforehand and this can be  stored in the fridge for up to a week so  try it out other easy and quick  pre-miracle snacks can include all kinds  of fruits cottage cheese with crackers  low sugar sports drink caffeine which is  going to boost your metabolism and to  improve performance endurance and many  different kinds of whole food which is  high in cups so let's move on to  post-workout meals and snacks your  post-workout meal is the first meal you  have after your workout session which is  also known as the anabolic phase having  the right post-workout meal will help  with increasing muscle mass to reduce  fatigue and muscle soreness and with  overall recovery to achieve this we want  to refill our body with high protein and  a little bit of carbs protein consists  of amino acids which build muscle and  help with recovering our muscle breaks  down during a workout and needs to be  rebuilt with protein for these reasons  we are encouraged to consume our  post-workout meals within 32  sixty minutes right after a workout  session this is when our body is most  ready to accept the carbs and protein  and to use these nutrients to reboot  restore and recover I like to schedule  my big meal right after a workout  session for instance I tend to work out  mid-morning and to have my lunch  straight after knowing that this is not  always possible for all of us I will be  sharing some examples of post-workout  snacks and meals that you can try out so  let's start with meals what I have here  is basic grilled chicken with veggies  your body is in recovery mode so you  need a nutrient-dense dish the lean  protein in the grilled chicken will fill  you up without feeling overly bloated  and the veggies are high in fiber and  they will keep you satisfied without  over eating the next meal is veggie  omelet what I have in here are broccolis  spinach carrots onions two eggs cooked  with a little bit of olive oil again  eggs are an easy source of protein they  are light on your body and they will  keep you satisfied and this is also a  great choice for vegetarians  another great post-workout meal is  salmon with sweet potato chips which is  my favorite because I love salmon and I  love sweet potatoes salmon is a great  source of protein with omega-3 and the  sweet potato chips is packed with  complex carbs which helps to restore  energy especially after an intense  workout if you are a vegan you can  always substitute the salmon or the  grilled chicken breast with beans or  even chickpeas so now let's move on to  some quick and light post-workout snacks  what I have here are tuna chunks and red  pepper hummus tuna is very low in  calories but high in protein 100 gram of  tuna only contains 99 calories and it  has 23 point five grams of protein  hummus is also low in calories and high  in protein and it is a great vegan  option too  feel your protein requirement so you can  either have tuna or hummus or both with  crackers or you can even make a sandwich  and pack it out with you so there is no  cooking required at all and this is  really convenient chocolate lovers this  is for you  recent research has shown that chocolate  milk is the latest craze in post-workout  snacks even over water and sports drink  this is because one cup of chocolate  milk has everything you need cups to  restore energy protein for muscle  recovery and water content to replace  lost fluid from exercisi